    {
      "id": "e05c3ada6f72-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "If \\(x^4+{1\\over x^4}=34\\) where \\(x>0\\) , then find the value of \\(x +{1\\over x}\\) .",
      "questionHtml": "If&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(x^4+{1\\over x^4}=34\\)</span>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(x&gt;0\\)</span>, then find the value of&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(x +{1\\over x}\\)</span>.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "\\(4\\sqrt2 \\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(4\\sqrt2 \\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "4.25",
          "html": "4.25"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "\\(2\\sqrt2 \\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(2\\sqrt2 \\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "4",
          "html": "4"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Formula:</strong></p>\n\n<p>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2 </sup>+ b<sup>2</sup> + 2ab</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>The given equation can be rearranged as-</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\((x^2)^2+({1\\over x^2})^2 +2 × x^2 × {1\\over x^2}=34+2\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; (x<sup>2</sup> + <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x^2\\)</span>)<sup>2</sup> = 36</p>\n\n<p>Taking square root both sides of the equation, we get-</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span style=\"\">x</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;+&nbsp;</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x^2\\)</span>&nbsp;= 6</p>\n\n<p>Again rearranging the equation as given below-</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; x<sup>2</sup> +&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x^2\\)</span> + 2&nbsp;&times; x &times; <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x \\)</span>&nbsp;= 6 + 2</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; (x +&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x \\)</span>&nbsp;)<sup>2 </sup>= 8</p>\n\n<p>Taking square root both sides, we get-</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span style=\"\">x +&nbsp;</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x \\)</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;= &radic;8 or 2&radic;2</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&there4;<strong> The value of&nbsp;</strong></span><strong><span style=\"\">​</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(x +{1\\over x}\\)</span><span style=\"\">​ is&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;2&radic;2.</span></strong></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\"><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Shortcut Trick</u></span></strong></span>&nbsp;</span></strong><span style=\"\">If x<sup>4</sup>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x^4\\)</span>&nbsp;= n&nbsp;then</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">x<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x^2\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\sqrt{n+2}\\)</span></span>&nbsp;= p</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">x +&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x \\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\sqrt{p+2}\\)</span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Now,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">x<sup>2&nbsp;</sup>+&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x^2\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\sqrt{34+2}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\sqrt36\\)</span>&nbsp;= 6</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">And, x +&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x \\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\sqrt{6+2}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\sqrt8\\)</span></span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(2\\sqrt2\\)</span>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The value of x +&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1\\over x \\)</span>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(2\\sqrt2\\)</span>.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e05c3ada6f72-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "Which of the following statement is correct? I. If x = 12, y = -2 and z = -10, then x 3 + y 3 + z 3 = 360. II. If x + y = 48 and 4xy = 128, then 4x 2 + 4y 2 = 4480.",
      "questionHtml": "<p style=\"\">Which of the following statement is correct?</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">I. If x = 12, y = -2 and z = -10, then x<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">3</span>&nbsp;+ y<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">3</span>&nbsp;+ z<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">3</span>&nbsp;= 360.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">II.&nbsp;If x&nbsp;+&nbsp;y = 48 and 4xy = 128, then 4x<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;+ 4y<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;= 4480.</p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Neither I nor II",
          "html": "Neither I nor II"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Only I",
          "html": "Only I"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Both I and II",
          "html": "Both I and II"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Only II",
          "html": "Only II"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Statement I.  x<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">3</span> + y<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">3</span> + z<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">3</span>  ⇒ (12)<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">3</span> + (-2)<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">3</span> + (-10)<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">3</span>  ⇒ 1728 - 8 - 1000 ⇒ 720</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Statement II. (2</span>x)<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> + (2y)<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> = (2x + 2y)<sup>2</sup> - 8xy = (2× 48)<sup>2</sup> - 2× 128 = 9216 - 256 = 8960</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Hence, n</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">either I nor II follows.</span></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e05c3ada6f72-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "\\(\\frac{(941+149)^2+(941-149)^2}{941\\times 941+149\\times 149}\\)",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{(941+149)^2+(941-149)^2}{941\\times 941+149\\times 149}\\)</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "2",
          "html": "2"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "-2",
          "html": "-2"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "0",
          "html": "0"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "1",
          "html": "1"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png' width='26px' /> <u style='font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; display: inline !important;'>Shortcut Trick</u></span>\n<p>Identify the standard <strong>algebraic identity</strong> pattern in the given expression:</p>\n<p><strong>((a + b)<sup>2</sup> + (a − b)<sup>2</sup>) ÷ (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)</strong></p>\n<p>By algebraic properties, the numerator simplifies to: <strong>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> + (a − b)<sup>2</sup> = 2(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)</strong>.</p>\n<p>Substituting this back, we get: <strong>2(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>) ÷ (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>) = 2</strong>, which is independent of the values of <strong>a</strong> and <strong>b</strong>.</p>\n<p>Here, <strong>a = 941</strong> and <strong>b = 149</strong>, so the expression simplifies directly to <strong>2</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 2.</strong></p><p><span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png' width='26px' /><strong><span style='vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;'><u>Alternate Method</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n<p>Expression: ((941 + 149)<sup>2</sup> + (941 − 149)<sup>2</sup>) ÷ (941 × 941 + 149 × 149)</p>\n<p>Let <strong>a = 941</strong> and <strong>b = 149</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Formula Used:</strong></p>\n<p>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + 2ab + b<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p>(a − b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> − 2ab + b<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n<p>⇒ Numerator = (941 + 149)<sup>2</sup> + (941 − 149)<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p>⇒ Numerator = (a + b)<sup>2</sup> + (a − b)<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p>⇒ Numerator = (a<sup>2</sup> + 2ab + b<sup>2</sup>) + (a<sup>2</sup> − 2ab + b<sup>2</sup>)</p>\n<p>⇒ Numerator = 2a<sup>2</sup> + 2b<sup>2</sup> = 2(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)</p>\n<p>⇒ Denominator = 941 × 941 + 149 × 149 = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p>⇒ Expression = Numerator ÷ Denominator</p>\n<p>⇒ Expression = 2(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>) ÷ (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)</p>\n<p>⇒ Expression = 2</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 2.</strong></p><p><span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png' width='26px' /><strong><span style='vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;'><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Sum of Squares Identity</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>The sum of the squares of the sum and difference of two numbers is represented as <strong>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> + (a − b)<sup>2</sup> = 2(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)</strong>.</p>\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Difference of Squares Identity</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>The difference of the squares of the sum and difference of two numbers is represented as <strong>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> − (a − b)<sup>2</sup> = 4ab</strong>.</p>\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Standard Algebraic Ratio Rule</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>For any real values of a and b, the quotient of <strong>((a + b)<sup>2</sup> − (a − b)<sup>2</sup>) ÷ ab</strong> is always equal to <strong>4</strong>.</p>",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
