          "id": "D",
          "text": "-2197",
          "html": "-2197"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Let's assume that (r/13) = x</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">According to the question: ⇒ <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{r}{13} + \\frac{13}{r} = 1\\)</span><span style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-size: var(--bs-body-font-size); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\"> ⇒ x + 1/x = 1</span>, then x<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">3</span> = - 1</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now, putting the value of x ⇒ (r/13)<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">3</span> = - 1 ⇒ r<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">3</span> = - 2197</p>\n",
